th on the streets and on social  media  with people now demanding the release of  arrested protesters  and justice for deceased victims  but kingsley doesn't believe that  dissolving stars will end police  brutality  in the country when you put a rotten egg  among good ones just give it a little  time  the good ones are not going to make the  bad one good rather the bad one is going  to make the good ones bad  let me suppress them and speak to  nigerians  we want to hear him want to feel that he  feels the pain we are going through  even if you're lying just say something  to us the founder of the movement  and sars who started the first online  campaign in 2016  is encouraging people on twitter to keep  on demonstrating  he doesn't want the protests to fizzle  out this time  without real reform  and earlier i spoke to sheikh unawa  sonya who's  mentioned there he's from the nsar's  online campaign  he's been pushing to have nigeria's  special anti-robbery squad disbanded  for years i asked him why demonstrators  are staying on the streets to protest  even after the government announced that  sars would be dissolved  justices are on the street because they  felt that this is just another political  pronouncement  and they want to be certain they need  assurances that did for this time around  that they are going to actually get what  they are asking for for many years from  2015 we've been caring about the  disbandment of serve  the evolution of sas and several other  things and it has not materialized on  ground  so this time around they want to be sure  that um  it's they are going for it that's why  they are demanding for a presidential  order  in that regard so despite the  announcement that's a  clearly a lack of trust in the police  and government  definitely the the trust in the police  have been  winged over the years because of um  violation of human rights and also  because of many things that  has been promised that was never kept  okay  um so if these pr